## Environment tfvars (AC 7: independent deployment)

```hcl
# environments/dev.tfvars
environment                 = "dev"
aws_region                  = "us-east-1"
cluster_node_count          = 2
cluster_instance_type       = "t3.medium"
db_instance_class           = "db.t3.micro"
db_multi_az                 = false
bucket_replication_region   = null   # no replication in dev
```

```hcl
# environments/prod.tfvars
environment                 = "prod"
aws_region                  = "us-east-1"
cluster_node_count          = 4
cluster_instance_type       = "t3.large"
db_instance_class           = "db.t3.medium"
db_multi_az                 = true
bucket_replication_region   = "us-west-2"
cluster_oidc_provider_arn   = "arn:aws:iam::111111111111:oidc-provider/oidc.eks.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/id/EXAMPLE"
```

Alternatively, use **workspaces**: prefix resources with `terraform.workspace` and drive sizes from a `map` lookup. tfvars files keep dev/prod in *separate state backends* (override `backend "s3"` key with `-backend-config="key=app/${ENV}.tfstate"`), which more strictly guarantees AC 7.

## Usage

```bash
# Prod
terraform init -backend-config="key=app/prod.tfstate"
terraform plan -var-file=environments/prod.tfvars -out prod.plan
terraform apply prod.plan

# Dev
terraform init -backend-config="key=app/dev.tfstate" -reconfigure
terraform plan -var-file=environments/dev.tfvars -out dev.plan
terraform apply dev.plan
```

## Acceptance Criteria Mapping

| AC | How satisfied |
|---|---|
| 1 Bucket | `aws_s3_bucket_versioning`, SSE-KMS with rotation, full public access block |
| 2 RDS | `deletion_protection = true`, retention 14 days, `publicly_accessible = false`, private subnets |
| 3 Secret | Random password → Secrets Manager (KMS-encrypted); nothing plaintext in code or tfvars |
| 4 IAM | Scoped actions only, prod restricts by key prefix and OIDC subject; zero wildcards |
| 5 Cluster | Node counts/types from tfvars (2×t3.medium vs 4×t3.large); EKS module usage omitted but parameterized |
| 6 HTTPS | CloudFront distribution with ACM cert referenced via `variables` when EKS/CloudFront module is wired; ALB listeners stay 443 |
| 7 Isolation | Separate state backends + separate account roles per environment |

**Note:** The EKS cluster and ALB/CloudFront stacks are consumed via `terraform-aws-modules/eks/aws` and `terraform-aws-modules/alb/aws`, sized by the same tfvars (`cluster_node_count`, `cluster_instance_type`) shown above; they were abbreviated to keep focus on the requested S3/RDS/IAM modules.
